==ClassicAPI Addons==
These addons either require the [https://github.com/brues-code/ClassicAPI ClassicAPI] [https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Client_Fixes_and_Tweaks client mod] to work, or provide more features with ClassicAPI.

===== '''What is ClassicAPI?''' =====
*ClassicAPI is [https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Client_Fixes_and_Tweaks client mod] that backports the modern WoW API to the turtle wow 1.12 client. This means addon developers have more options for creating features and performance optimizations.
*It also provides some quality of life improvements like modern macro syntax (#showtooltip). The github README provides extensive documentation on its features.

===== '''How do I install ClassicAPI?''' =====
#ClassicAPI is a mod that uses a code injection DLL to modify the client. Antivirus software often flags these as malicious. This is normal, just allow them on device. If you are concerned about this, you can do take the downloaded zip file and upload it on [https://www.virustotal.com/gui/home/upload Virustotal]. If very few services flag it as malicious, that is a sign of false positive detection, which means it is actually safe.
#ClassicAPI requires [https://github.com/hannesmann/vanillafixes VanillaFixes] to run. Install the [https://github.com/hannesmann/vanillafixes/releases latest version].
#Copy all the files into your WoW folder, where your wow.exe is located. DO NOT put the files inside the Addons folder. If you already have dlls.txt, do not overwrite it, the rest of the files can be overwritten.
#Open the dlls.txt file, and make sure it has a line with "ClassicAPI.dll" (no "#"). If it lists DLLs you don't have installed in that same directory, that's fine.
#Now you can download the ClassicAPI.dll from the [https://github.com/brues-code/ClassicAPI/releases latest release] and place it in the same directory as your wow.exe.
#Start the game using a launcher or by running VanillaFixes.exe in your WoW folder. If you get a popup window showing DLLs that will load, click OK.
#In the login screen, open the Addons menu and check if !!!ClassicAPI is there. If yes, then you're done.

